# scripts/harness_caps.env — SHARED constants for the auto-memory index guards
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by BOTH scripts/check_memory_length.sh (source) and
# scripts/memory_index_check.py (line-parse), so the two guards can never
# disagree on what "the cap" is.
#
# Root canon 1d: the Claude Code harness auto-loads the first ~200 lines /
# ~25,600 bytes of memory/auto/MEMORY.md at boot; anything past that is
# silently dropped (no warning).
#
# Provenance: born 2026-08-14 (DAEDALUS, scripts/ lane) off PROME's ask
# after DEWEY's 8/12 flag — the same file read "82% of cap" (py) and "77%"
# (sh) in the SAME closeout because the two tools compared against different
# constants (24,400 vs 25,600). PAT-069 (interface property) shape:
# "the cap" is a concept, each tool resolved a different instrument.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, no spaces, no quotes, no expansion — safe to `source`
# in bash and safe to line-parse in python. If you add a key, keep it
# valid in both.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The real harness caps (root canon 1d).
MEMORY_HARNESS_CAP_BYTES=25600
MEMORY_HARNESS_CAP_LINES=200

# Soft-warn triggers (percent-of-hard, INTEGER — do not float).
# One number, two units: applied to bytes and to lines identically.
# 75% = the Will-approved FLOW RULE (2026-08-12): at >=75% of the byte cap PROME
# demotes rows to the cold index until <70%. RE-KEYED 2026-08-28 (DAEDALUS, 8/28
# wiring sweep; found by MIDAS, verified by PROME + BOND): the guard sat at 80%
# from 2026-08-03, the rule landed at 75% on 8/12, and nobody re-keyed the guard —
# so for 75-80% both tools printed "OK: under the cap" while the ruled ratchet was
# FIRING (measured live 8/27 at 76.9%; BOND watched it climb 74->76% across three
# closeout runs, all "OK"). finding_a_ruling_governs_the_next_write_not_the_existing_state,
# tool edition. The warn tier now IS the rule's trip line.
MEMORY_WARN_PERCENT=75

# Per-slug hook length canon (chars). MEMORY.md rows may run inline after
# a slug as ` — hook text …`. This is the target length the writer should
# stay under; the guard warns above, never fails. 80 matches the fleet
# canon PROME cited (measured driver of the index's ~535 B/day growth was
# appended hooks running 150–250 B).
MEMORY_HOOK_WARN_CHARS=80
